# Docs: Anatomy

When a **ComponentPage** documents a Vira surface with **consumer-composable `.` parts**, a **multi-part compose tree**, or a **forced host** that must combine with sibling components, put `## Anatomy` **after the lead** thematic break and **before** `## When to use`. Contract: `specs/001-llm-first-docs-site/contracts/page-shell.md`.

## When required

- Public compound attachments (`Object.assign` / namespace) such as `Dialog.Trigger`, `Menu.Popup`, `Select.Option`, `Skeleton.Overlay`
- Co-exported part trees composed under a domain root (e.g. `Gauge` + `GaugeTrack` / `GaugeArc` / …)
- Forced hosts that nest sibling components as children (e.g. `ToggleGroup` + `ToggleButton` / `ToggleTextButton`)

## When omit

- True leaves: standalone single export with no `.` parts and no required sibling host (Button, Stack, Meter, …)
- Prop-driven hosts with no child compose tree (e.g. `AvatarGroup` — `avatars` array maps to Avatar; not compound Anatomy)
- Hub `content/components/index.mdx`

## Authority (do not invent)

1. Sibling DS `packages/react/src/components/<id>/` public `Object.assign` / namespace / index co-exports / required sibling hosts
2. Consumer skill shapes in `../viraui-skills/skills/viraui-design/composition.md` when present
3. Never invent Portal/backdrop/chrome that is baked into a public part (e.g. Dialog portal lives inside `Sheet`)
4. Never invent child APIs the surface does not expose
5. Never generate Anatomy from `patterns.xml` (usage examples, not part trees)

## Shape

```mdx
## Anatomy

Import the component and assemble its parts:

```tsx
import { Dialog } from '@viraui/react';

<Dialog.Provider>
  <Dialog.IndentBackground>
    <Dialog.Indent>
      <Dialog>
        <Dialog.Trigger />
        <Dialog.Sheet>
          <Dialog.Close />
        </Dialog.Sheet>
      </Dialog>
    </Dialog.Indent>
  </Dialog.IndentBackground>
</Dialog.Provider>
```

---
```

Forced-compose host (no `.` parts; documented on the host or the child page that teaches the group):

```tsx
import { ToggleButton, ToggleGroup, ToggleTextButton } from '@viraui/react';

<ToggleGroup>
  <ToggleButton />
  <ToggleTextButton />
</ToggleGroup>
```

## Rules

- One fence only — import + nested skeleton, **no props**, self-closing parts
- Include the full public tree / forced-compose set — **no** `{/* optional */}` markers
- Hooks / factories that are not DOM parts (`createToastManager`, `useFilter`, `createHandle`) stay **out** of the tree; one short prose line under the fence only when the page already teaches them
- After Anatomy, thematic break (`---`) before When to use / next section
- Structure only — not a prop inventory or surface catalog
